.SH NAME
le-check - HTTP health-check a listener (status + latency + curl)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle check PORT [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
GET http://127.0.0.1:PORT/ and report the status code and round-trip
time, plus a ready-to-run curl command. A non-HTTP listener surfaces as
a clear error rather than hanging.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for check


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


